# Waves demo for the loaded build hk8s32u32n1i1024 (8 blocks, 32 lanes).  Run it with:  batch batches/waves_demo.score
# Part 1: 300 independent jobs of 40 words each.  The far RAM setting is held small on purpose, so the design needs several waves
# (the card itself has 65,536 words; the front end plans for the number you set).  Each wave is an ordinary run; the answers of all
# 300 jobs are put together and compared at the end.
use hk8s32u32n1i1024
set lw 5
new
many 300 vsum seq 1 40 1
set far-words 0x3000
waves
run
# Part 2: a pipeline.  Stage 1 sums 100 numbers, stage 2 scales that answer, stage 3 sums the result.  Each stage is run only after
# the stage before has been read back, and is fed the card's own answer.
new
set far-words none
set lw 0
add vsum seq 1 100 1
add vscale from=0 arg=3
add vsum from=1
waves
run
